  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "We prove Markey's conjecture in OEIS A400701, FORMULA, revision 30 (October 20, 2026), that the five-site growth count exceeds Shannon's circle-vertex count at the same iteration n > 1 by 4n+7, using residue-class points in expanding hexagons. Counting incidences on the same shapes also proves Shannon's conjectured region formulas and gives the curved-edge counts. The argument proves the recorded formulas for three and four initial sites and the generating functions recorded by Irvine.",
